[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4368639811","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119087#issuecomment-4368639811","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119087","id":4368639811,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBGQnQw","user":{"login":"CD-DA","id":145823278,"node_id":"U_kgDOCLEWLg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145823278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA","html_url":"https://github.com/CD-DA","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T06:00:37Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T06:19:32Z","body":"I set a breakpoint at `EditorSettingsDialog::_event_config_confirmed()`, and of the different problem scenarios, it seems like they all eventually lead to `InputEventConfigurationDialog::_set_event()` right before calling `AcceptDialog::_ok_pressed()` (which then goes on to match the normal route).\n\n`InputEventConfigurationDialog::_set_event()` appears to have special hard coded scenarios for the `ENTER` and `ESCAPE` keys which are not present in the 4.6 branch.\n\nI think this also means the problem extends to the escape key, but maybe it would effect things differently since `_cancel_pressed()` gets called instead of `_ok_pressed()`.\n\nEdit: Seems like it effects the escape key as well, but instead of auto submitting it auto cancels. I think this might be related to #116625?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4368639811/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4369189079","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119087#issuecomment-4369189079","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119087","id":4369189079,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBGyI1w","user":{"login":"CD-DA","id":145823278,"node_id":"U_kgDOCLEWLg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145823278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA","html_url":"https://github.com/CD-DA","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T07:55:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T07:55:16Z","body":"Looks like the bug happens due to how the function `InputEventConfigurationDialog::_set_event()` is set up.\n\nWhen a new input dialog appears, a variable `event` is set to a blank input event.\nOn our first input, this `event` variable is set to whatever that input was.\nOn our second input, `event` is now valid which means we pass the `event.is_valid()` and then check if our new key is either `ENTER` or `ESCAPE` to exit the dialog.\n\nEssentially it seems like if our second input is either `ENTER` or `ESCAPE`, the dialog will close out. (which is a little strange, since the case where we press the shift check box shouldn't broadcast an enter key right?)\n\nPerhaps there is a better way to fix this, but it seems like making the exit keys more complex might be necessary (like a ctrl + escape). ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4369189079/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4370597043","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119087#issuecomment-4370597043","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119087","id":4370597043,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBIIEsw","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T11:18:18Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:18:18Z","body":"> I think this might be related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116625?\n\nThat's definitely the cause. The current behavior isn't very friendly.\n\nCC @Goldenlion5648 ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4370597043/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4371311821","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119087#issuecomment-4371311821","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119087","id":4371311821,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBIzszQ","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T13:11:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T13:11:17Z","body":"@KoBeWi So do you want the behavior to be updated to require the current in \"event configuration dialog\" to be something other than the default \"listening for event\" in order for the UI to close?\n\n<img width=\"1914\" height=\"1048\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e249aaf1-5360-40af-8b5e-08f2c406d247\" />\n\nI also see there is a bug when trying to bind something like \"shift + enter\". \n\nThe intent of my PR was to allow quicker binding of keybinds (which people seemed to like based on the reactions/ comments). How much of the (intended) changes from my PR do you want to keep?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4371311821/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4371693684","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119087#issuecomment-4371693684","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119087","id":4371693684,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBJLAdA","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T14:04:46Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:04:46Z","body":"It might be enough if LineEdit required focus to use Enter as accept. It would at least allow to navigate the key list.\n\nAs for not being able to assign Enter, it's not really intuitive that you need empty event to assign Enter. But it's mostly a problem when editing an action, not when adding a new one. I don't have a solution in mind that would allow both assigning and accepting, other than maybe hold to accept.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4371693684/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4372379561","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119087#issuecomment-4372379561","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119087","id":4372379561,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBJ03qQ","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","recei